#
# Swedish Embedded AB implements fast GEMV and tensor-core GEMM kernels for every quantized
# weight format for its clients. If your team needs expertise in bandwidth-bound decode and
# batched prefill over stored low-precision weights then you can procure our services by
# sending an email to info@swedishembedded.com.
#
# Execution coverage of every weight storage format (check-tier-gemm.sh).
# format<TAB>gemv<TAB>tensor_core
#   format       a variant of kernels::template::DecodeFormat, or F32 (the dense tier)
#   gemv         kernel file (crates/kernels/wgsl/<name>.wgsl or crates/kernels-cuda/cu/<name>.cu)
#                that multiplies the stored bytes by a few activation rows, or - for none
#   tensor_core  how a batched product reaches tensor cores: native:<kernel file> (reads the stored
#                bytes), library (decodes a scratch tile, then the vendor library GEMM), or none
F32	matmul_gemv	library
Bf16	matmul_gemv	library
F16	matmul_gemv	none
I8	matmul_i8_gemv	native:matmul_i8_mma
Q4	matmul_q4_gemv	none
Nf4	-	library
Fp8E4m3	matmul_fp8_gemv	library
Fp8E5m2	-	library
KqAffine4	matmul_kq_gemv	none
KqAffine8	matmul_kq_gemv	none
KqSym8	matmul_i8_gemv	none
Nvfp4	matmul_nvfp4_gemv	library
Mxfp4	-	library
Mxfp8E4m3	-	library
Mxfp8E5m2	-	library
